/**
 * @mainpage KymoCore embedded API
 *
 * @brief Portable C++11 telemetry with caller-owned storage and configurable I/O.
 *
 * @section lifecycle Configuration and lifecycle
 * Define persistent channel descriptors, mutable channel state and a KymoConfig.
 * Supply clock, sample and write callbacks; provide service and busy callbacks when
 * required by the transport. Call Kymo_Init once and Kymo_Main cyclically
 * from one task. Keep the configuration and referenced objects alive while the
 * context is in use. The runtime never allocates heap storage.
 *
 * @code{.c}
 * // Application configuration implements callbacks and owns persistent storage.
 * static KymoContext context;
 * void application_init(void)
 * {
 *     KymoStatus status = Kymo_Init(&context, &application_config);
 *     // Handle status before enabling the periodic application task.
 * }
 * void application_cycle(void)
 * {
 *     KymoStatus status = Kymo_Main(&context);
 *     // Handle transport/configuration errors; continue cyclic calls on BUSY.
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section modules API areas
 * - Pass build-wide feature definitions or KYMO_USER_CONFIG_HEADER; kymo_config.h
 *   validates them. Keep the release submodule unchanged. Defaults enable scalar encoding
 *   and Init/Main only; X/Z/time, CRC, MCU decoding and C++ are opt-in.
 * - @ref kymo_runtime describes configuration, callbacks and runtime state.
 * - See the module index for the wire codec, common byte/bit/CRC operations,
 *   optional C++ wrapper and application-side hardware adapters.
 * - Each header documents its macros, types, members and callable interfaces.
 *   Function parameters include direction, valid inputs and ownership. Usage
 *   sections describe how to apply constants, fields and functions.
 *
 * @section contracts Execution and transport contracts
 * Calls are non-reentrant. Synchronize interrupt-shared data in the application.
 * A successful write reports driver acceptance, not physical delivery. Short
 * writes preserve remaining bytes for later cycles. For zero-copy asynchronous
 * transfers, busy must remain true until the driver releases the buffer.
 * Clock values and channel periods are in milliseconds. Read each callback's
 * detailed contract before adapting UART, USB, TCP or another byte transport.
 *
 * @section portability Portability and scope
 * KymoCore has no Arduino or STM32 SDK dependencies. Hardware adapters belong
 * to examples/application code. Headers under legacy and the independent Events
 * dependency are outside this API. The binary v6 wire format remains compatible
 * with KymoStudio; see lib/KymoCore/docs/PROTOCOL.md in the repository.
 * Documentation and single-exit style do not constitute safety certification.
 */

/* The released recorder exposes storage for static allocation. These members
 * are implementation state, not configurable Probe bindings. Document that
 * contract here without modifying the pinned third-party release checkout. */
/** @var KymoTraceContextState::id
 * @brief Internal recorder state; managed exclusively by KymoTrace APIs.
